0752100206445903,-1.3112935448589269e-05,-2.50339189733495e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,7824,315,279,444,324,352,356,33718,82,304,12989,6786,30161,1449,220,17,15,4420,13,8886,1899,304,5813,279,1156,7216,374,518,220,24,264,744,2572,323,279,1537,7216,8471,518,220,21,281,744,13,2585,1657,30161,525,1052,817,1899,304,5813,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe owners of the Luray Caverns in Virginia conduct tours every 20 minutes. Each day in April the first tour is at 9 a.m., and the last tour starts at 6 p.m. How many tours are there per day in April?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"4655308df82889783ae7e240eaa817f54ed6ccb2980d21adc8e78a5fa0bddb0f"},"seconds":19.472198009490967,"seed":624303528743358024,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of tours conducted each day in April by the Luray Caverns. Tours start every 20 minutes from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m.\n\n1. **Identify the start and end times:**\n   - First tour: 9 a.m.\n   - Last tour: 6 p.m.\n\n2. **Convert these times into a 24-hour format:**\n   - 9 a.m. is 09:00\n   - 6 p.m. is 18:00\n\n3. **Calculate the total duration between the first and last tours:**\n   - From 09:00 to 18:00 is a 9-hour period.\n\n4. **Convert this duration into minutes:**\n   - 9 hours * 60 minutes per hour = 540 minutes\n\n5. **Determine the number of 20-minute intervals within this period:**\n   - Number of 20-minute intervals = \\(\\frac{540 \\text{ minutes}}{20 \\text{ minutes per tour}} = 27\\)\n\n6. **Count the tours:**\n   - There are 27 intervals between the first and last tour, but we must include the first tour as well.\n   - Therefore, the total number of tours is \\(27 + 1 = 28\\).\n\nThus, the number of tours per day in April is \\(\\boxed{28}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{28}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
